but biblical peace is received through submission and obedience.

475
01:03:26,900 --> 01:03:32,900
A sheep without a shepherd can at times achieve peace through fighting or through avoiding, right?

476
01:03:32,900 --> 01:03:37,900
Through being aggressive or through avoiding any and all predators or from hiding or from being safe.

477
01:03:37,900 --> 01:03:41,900
They might achieve peace temporarily, and so it is with us.

478
01:03:41,900 --> 01:03:46,900
We might be able to achieve an experience of peace here and there from time to time,

479
01:03:46,900 --> 01:03:53,900
but in order for us to do that, we often have to fight back against our enemies or avoid our enemies altogether.

480
01:03:53,900 --> 01:03:58,900
Achieving peace on earth is an exhausting experience.

481
01:03:58,900 --> 01:04:01,900
We have to fight for it.

482
01:04:01,900 --> 01:04:05,900
We have to work hard for it, and the moment that we think we have it,

483
01:04:05,900 --> 01:04:09,900
there's something lurking in the background that we feel like might take it away.

484
01:04:09,900 --> 01:04:15,900
Earthly peace is fleeting and exhausting because it constantly has to be achieved.

485
01:04:15,900 --> 01:04:23,900
And I said aggressive, but some of us in here maybe achieve it through passive aggressiveness.

486
01:04:23,900 --> 01:04:24,900
Right?

487
01:04:24,900 --> 01:04:25,900
You're like, that's not me.

488
01:04:25,900 --> 01:04:26,900
I don't fight back.

489
01:04:26,900 --> 01:04:27,900
Hmm.

490
01:04:27,900 --> 01:04:28,900
All right.

491
01:04:28,900 --> 01:04:30,900
Well, let's throw in there passive aggressive for you as well.

492
01:04:30,900 --> 01:04:31,900
Right?

493
01:04:31,900 --> 01:04:35,900
Like there's this way we go about trying to find peace.

494
01:04:35,900 --> 01:04:39,900
If someone insults us, we insult them back.

495
01:04:39,900 --> 01:04:41,900
Someone gossips, we return the favor.

496
01:04:41,900 --> 01:04:43,900
An eye for an eye.

497
01:04:43,900 --> 01:04:55,900
But here's the problem with that approach is that if your goal is peace, you cannot stop fighting back until you've overpowered every person or thing that is in the way of your peace.

498
01:04:55,900 --> 01:05:00,900
Always looking over your shoulder for the next threat, just like a sheep without a shepherd.

499
01:05:00,900 --> 01:05:07,900
You might be able to experience pockets or periods of peace, but that peace will not last very long.

500
01:05:07,900 --> 01:05:23,900
If you feel like you don't have what you need, you don't have proper food or water sources, you work harder, you sacrifice more, you lose appreciation for what you have out of the pursuit of more constantly chasing that feeling of having what you think you need and never actually achieving it.

501
01:05:23,900 --> 01:05:30,900
Earthly peace, it can be achieved, but only temporarily through aggression or through avoidance.

502
01:05:30,900 --> 01:05:40,900
See, the alternative to fighting back would be my favorite approach, which is avoiding conflict altogether.

503
01:05:40,900 --> 01:05:44,900
Any peace keepers in the room or am I the only one?

504
01:05:44,900 --> 01:05:45,900
Cool.

505
01:05:45,900 --> 01:05:46,900
Just me.

506
01:05:46,900 --> 01:05:47,900
All right.

507
01:05:47,900 --> 01:05:48,900
Well, I wrote it in my notes.

508
01:05:48,900 --> 01:05:50,900
I'm going to read it anyway.

509
01:05:50,900 --> 01:06:00,900
The alternative to fighting back, to getting into conflict, to overpowering our enemies is to avoiding tension and conflict altogether, to totally running away from conflict.

510
01:06:00,900 --> 01:06:08,900
And again, we might experience partial peace this way, but it's draining because we actually aren't getting what we need.

511
01:06:08,900 --> 01:06:11,900
We're not being honest about the circumstances or realities of life.

512
01:06:11,900 --> 01:06:15,900
We're avoiding conflict that is there, pretending like it's not there.

513
01:06:15,900 --> 01:06:25,900
We might experience partial peace for temporary periods of time by avoiding or by being aggressive, but at the end of the day, it's temporary.

514
01:06:25,900 --> 01:06:40,900
A sheep without a shepherd, they might be able to avoid predators for a certain period of time, but eventually they will starve to death because in order to avoid predators, they have to put themselves far, far away from food sources, from food and water.

515
01:06:40,900 --> 01:06:52,900
And how often, even in our relationships, those of us who are avoidance people, how often do we actually not have what we need in the relationships that we want because we're not honest with the people we're in relationship with.

516
01:06:52,900 --> 01:06:54,900
Earthly peace.

517
01:06:54,900 --> 01:06:58,900
It can be achieved through aggression or avoidance, but it's temporary.

518
01:06:58,900 --> 01:06:59,900
It isn't lasting.

519
01:06:59,900 --> 01:07:05,900
On the other hand, biblical peace is secure because it isn't achieved by our efforts.

520
01:07:05,900 --> 01:07:18,900
Rather, it is received as we learn to submit and be obedient to the good shepherd, going where he wants us to go, even when it doesn't make sense.

521
01:07:18,900 --> 01:07:20,900
So, famous psalm.

522
01:07:20,900 --> 01:07:22,900
You guys might know where I'm going.

523
01:07:22,900 --> 01:07:33,900
King David, whose many of the messianic promises are rooted in a psalm that talks about peace as his experience as a shepherd.

524
01:07:33,900 --> 01:07:37,900
It says this in Psalm 23:1, "The Lord is my shepherd.

525
01:07:37,900 --> 01:07:39,900
I have all that I need.

526
01:07:39,900 --> 01:07:42,900
He lets me rest in green meadows.

527
01:07:42,900 --> 01:07:44,900
He leads me beside peaceful streams.

528
01:07:44,900 --> 01:07:45,900
He renews my strength.

529
01:07:45,900 --> 01:07:48,900
He guides me along right paths, bringing honor to his name.

530
01:07:48,900 --> 01:07:53,900
Even when I walk through the darkest valley, I will not be afraid.

531
01:07:53,900 --> 01:07:55,900
For you are close behind me.

532
01:07:55,900 --> 01:07:59,900
Your rod and your staff, they protect and they comfort me.

533
01:07:59,900 --> 01:08:02,900
You prepare a feast before me in the presence of my enemies.

534
01:08:02,900 --> 01:08:04,900
You honor me by anointing my head with oil.

535
01:08:04,900 --> 01:08:07,900
My cup overflows with blessings.

536
01:08:07,900 --> 01:08:13,900
Surely your goodness and unfailing love will pursue me all the days of my life.

537
01:08:13,900 --> 01:08:18,900
And I will live in the house of the Lord forever."

538
01:08:19,900 --> 01:08:26,900
This is David poetically explaining what he feels like it is to be led by Yahweh as good shepherd.

539
01:08:26,900 --> 01:08:37,900
As his own experience of leading his sheep to places of peace, of having a plan, of having an idea of where they're going, of knowing that he can protect them from danger.

540
01:08:37,900 --> 01:08:41,900
Knowing that he can lead them to the place of green pastures.

541
01:08:41,900 --> 01:08:45,900
He can get them through the darkest valleys to get them to the place where he needs to be.

542
01:08:45,900 --> 01:08:49,900
This is what it is to be led by God as a good shepherd.

543
01:08:51,900 --> 01:09:00,900
See, with a good shepherd, they don't feel the need to fight back because they have a good shepherd yielding a rod of justice.

544
01:09:00,900 --> 01:09:07,900
See, if we've been mistreated, if we've been abused, if we've been neglected, we don't have to fight back.

545
01:09:07,900 --> 01:09:14,900
Those of us that have submitted our lives to Jesus as the good shepherd, we know that our good shepherd is a good shepherd of justice.

546
01:09:14,900 --> 01:09:17,900
And ultimately, he will take care of all of the injustices in the world.

547
01:09:17,900 --> 01:09:19,900
We don't have to fight back against our enemies.

548
01:09:19,900 --> 01:09:25,900
We don't have to yield a rod because our shepherd yields a rod of justice.

549
01:09:25,900 --> 01:09:33,900
We don't have to avoid the dark valleys because we can entrust ourselves to his nurture and care.

550
01:09:33,900 --> 01:09:36,900
We know that he is going to lead us to the place that we need to go.

551
01:09:37,900 --> 01:09:45,900
We never get too far out of safety because we willingly receive correction from his gentle staff.

552
01:09:45,900 --> 01:09:46,900
He carries a rod and a staff.

553
01:09:46,900 --> 01:09:49,900
The rod is for our enemies and the staff is for us.

554
01:09:49,900 --> 01:09:56,900
When we get off track, when we move too far away from his plans or his purposes, he lovingly corrects us.

555
01:09:56,900 --> 01:10:00,900
And if we're willing to receive that correction, we will never get too far out of safety.

556
01:10:01,900 --> 01:10:04,900
Because he has our best interest in mind.

557
01:10:04,900 --> 01:10:08,900
The Lord is our shepherd.

558
01:10:08,900 --> 01:10:12,900
We have all that we need.

559
01:10:12,900 --> 01:10:15,900
Isn't that the definition of peace?

560
01:10:15,900 --> 01:10:16,900
Isn't that biblical shalom?

561
01:10:16,900 --> 01:10:19,900
Wholeness, completeness, having everything that we need.

562
01:10:19,900 --> 01:10:24,900
If we want peace, we have to stop trying to achieve it through our own means

563
01:10:24,900 --> 01:10:31,900
and we have to sit back and allow Jesus as our good shepherd to lead us through the circumstances of our life

564
01:10:31,900 --> 01:10:33,900
and to bring about peace for us.

565
01:10:33,900 --> 01:10:41,900
Remember at the beginning of my short talk, I was referencing the most famous Christmas passage about peace.

566
01:10:41,900 --> 01:10:46,900
Well, there's one other Christmas passage about peace that we read a lot.

567
01:10:46,900 --> 01:10:49,900
And we've read it last week in the angel's announcement to the shepherd.

568
01:10:49,900 --> 01:10:58,900
It says this, "Glory to God in the highest heaven and peace on earth to those with whom God is well pleased."

569
01:10:58,900 --> 01:11:04,900
I don't think it's ironic that the first official announcement of the birth of the good shepherd

570
01:11:04,900 --> 01:11:11,900
was announced to shepherds who provided peace for their flock, but had no one to provide peace for them.

571
01:11:11,900 --> 01:11:18,900
These shepherds were themselves like sheep without a shepherd, but everything was about to change.

572
01:11:18,900 --> 01:11:21,900
This announcement is the beginning of what Ezekiel prophesied.

573
01:11:21,900 --> 01:11:27,900
God himself came looking for his scattered flock, and he is still doing so today.

574
01:11:27,900 --> 01:11:36,900
We have a good shepherd who is gathering for himself his flock who are willing to submit and to obey him,

575
01:11:36,900 --> 01:11:39,900
even when it doesn't make sense.

576
01:11:39,900 --> 01:11:42,900
Even when he has us walk through the valley of the shadow of death.

577
01:11:42,900 --> 01:11:48,900
Are we willing to submit and obey him, even when our enemies fight back against us?

578
01:11:48,900 --> 01:11:52,900
Even when the circumstances of our life are not leading us to have the things that we need?

579
01:11:52,900 --> 01:11:54,900
Are we willing to trust him?

580
01:11:54,900 --> 01:11:58,900
This is what the Bible says, that we can have a peace that passes understanding

581
01:11:58,900 --> 01:12:01,900
if we willingly submit and obey Jesus.

582
01:12:01,900 --> 01:12:06,900
So are you exhausted from trying to achieve peace on your own?

583
01:12:06,900 --> 01:12:08,900
Stop fighting your enemies.

584
01:12:08,900 --> 01:12:10,900
Love them.

585
01:12:10,900 --> 01:12:15,900
Pray for them and entrust yourself to the good shepherd who yields the rod of justice.

586
01:12:15,900 --> 01:12:18,900
Justice is his job, not ours.

587
01:12:20,900 --> 01:12:25,900
Stop avoiding conflicts or trials and step into them with grace and truth.

588
01:12:25,900 --> 01:12:29,900
Be honest with the people around you about the things that they're doing that hurt you,

589
01:12:29,900 --> 01:12:32,900
but do so with grace and with truth.

590
01:12:32,900 --> 01:12:35,900
Don't avoid conflict, but lean into it with the grace of God.

591
01:12:35,900 --> 01:12:42,900
The good shepherd will lead you through the shadow of the valley of death and into greener pastures.

592
01:12:45,900 --> 01:12:50,900
Our good shepherd has something so much more for us than just the absence of conflict or tension.

593
01:12:50,900 --> 01:12:54,900
Again, when we submit our lives to Jesus as the good shepherd.

594
01:12:54,900 --> 01:12:58,900
Excuse me, wow.

595
01:12:58,900 --> 01:13:04,900
Psalm 23 says, "He will give us all that we need."

596
01:13:04,900 --> 01:13:07,900
This is shalom, this is true peace.

597
01:13:07,900 --> 01:13:13,900
When we give up our ability to earn it for ourselves and when we sit back and receive it from God.

598
01:13:14,900 --> 01:13:18,900
Biblical peace is received through submission and obedience to Jesus as our good shepherd.

599
01:13:18,900 --> 01:13:20,900
Let's pray.

600
01:13:20,900 --> 01:13:22,900
Father in heaven.

601
01:13:22,900 --> 01:13:27,900
We thank you that you give us all that we need.

602
01:13:27,900 --> 01:13:33,900
And we acknowledge that we are so easily tempted to try and go get it for ourselves.

603
01:13:33,900 --> 01:13:35,900
To try and fight back against our enemies.

604
01:13:35,900 --> 01:13:37,900
To try and avoid conflict at all costs.

605
01:13:37,900 --> 01:13:40,900
To try and hold things together as much as we can.

606
01:13:41,900 --> 01:13:44,900
Let's get through this holiday season and then we can take a deep breath.

607
01:13:44,900 --> 01:13:45,900
No, that is false peace.

608
01:13:45,900 --> 01:13:47,900
That does not last.

609
01:13:47,900 --> 01:13:52,900
God, may we receive from you a lasting peace that passes all understanding.

610
01:13:52,900 --> 01:13:56,900
May we be willing to submit our lives to you.

611
01:13:56,900 --> 01:14:00,900
May we be willing to follow you even when it doesn't make sense.

612
01:14:01,900 --> 01:14:02,900
May we be willing to do this for us.

613
01:14:02,900 --> 01:14:03,900
May we be willing to do this for us.

614
01:14:03,900 --> 01:14:04,900
May we be willing to do this for us.

615
01:14:37,900 --> 01:14:38,900
Have a great week.

616
01:14:38,900 --> 01:14:39,900
And hopefully we'll see you in a couple of days.

617
01:14:39,900 --> 01:14:41,900
For our Christmas Eve service.

618
01:15:07,900 --> 01:15:08,900
May we be willing to do this for us.

619
01:15:08,900 --> 01:15:09,900
May we be willing to do this for us.

620
01:15:09,900 --> 01:15:10,900
May we be willing to do this for us.
